# Build subdirectories.
/*build*
!/build-aux
!/build_msvc

*.pyc

# Only ignore unexpected patches
*.patch
!contrib/guix/patches/*.patch
!depends/patches/**/*.patch

/CMakeUserPresets.json

# Previous releases
/releases

#build tests
test/lint/test_runner/target/

/guix-build-*

/ci/scratch/

# PCoin: never publish credentials from this public repo
PCOIN-SECRETS.md
# Fleet inventories name SSH accounts, key paths and device IDs. They live on
# D: with the other secrets; these patterns are the net under the tightrope,
# not permission to keep a copy here.
MYMINERS.md
PCOIN-SERVERS.md
*SERVERS.md
*SECRETS*
*credential*
*.key
*.pem
wallet.dat
*wallet-backup*
# Signing material. contrib/android/.gitignore covers the app tree, but a
# keystore dropped anywhere else in the repo would sail straight past it, and
# this repo is public.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
signing.properties
local.properties
# Build chatter, not source.
contrib/windows-tray/build.log

# pcoin-seed-vault writes its output into the working directory, so a run
# started from inside a clone would otherwise leave an encrypted wallet backup
# staged for commit. Encrypted is not published: the blob plus a guessed
# passphrase is the money, and a public repo is the wrong place to start that
# race. The xpub is harmless but is excluded too, because a wallet's full
# deposit history is nobody else's business.
*-seed.enc.json
*-xpub.txt
# Anything else this project encrypts, by shape rather than by name. The rule
# above is `*-seed.enc.json`, which did NOT match pcoin-bundle.enc.json — a
# 9.5 MB blob holding the release keystore, the TLS private key, every wallet
# backup and the retired seed phrases. It sat untracked and stageable until
# someone looked. A pattern that only catches the file you thought of is not a
# net, so this catches the shape.
*.enc.json
# Pool listings are only public addresses, so this is privacy rather than
# custody: one file linking every address a system will ever issue hands an
# observer the whole deposit history in one read.
*-pool-*.txt
contrib/vault/node_modules/


# Icon generator scratch output. The SVG/PNG/ICO that actually ship are tracked
# in contrib/branding/ and contrib/windows-tray/; this is just the working dir.
contrib/branding/out/

# Live server credentials — the repo is PUBLIC. Never track this.
servers.md
ARCHITECTURE.puml
SYSTEM-README.md

# ops dashboard: real config holds the scrypt hash, session secret and
# collector token; state.json is runtime data. Only the example is tracked.
contrib/ops-dashboard/config.json
contrib/ops-dashboard/state.json

# Built release artifacts -- produced by pack-win64.py, published to GitHub releases.
contrib/windows-tray/pcoin-win64-miner.zip
contrib/windows-tray/PCoinTray.exe
contrib/wpcn/wpcn.conf
contrib/wpcn/build/
contrib/wpcn/.venv/

# JVM crash dumps. A Gradle run that runs out of heap drops these in the repo
# root; the replay file alone was 856 KB. They are diagnostics for a crash that
# has already been read, never something to keep.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log


# CLAUDE.md is the project's orientation document and it names infrastructure:
# non-seed host IPs, which service runs where, deposit addresses and operational
# detail. That is fine on a private disk and wrong in a public repository, so it
# now lives at D:\pc.am\PCOIN-CLAUDE-MD.md and on both vault hosts.
#
# It stays on disk here on purpose -- Claude Code loads it from the project root,
# so ignoring it keeps every session's context while keeping it out of git.
CLAUDE.md
